# tone_atten (05-06; D-194, D-208, ER-15, ER-16): select 2 (table 2, F = 256) keyed on once (P1) and kept playing while the sc_atten script of the psg_tone.s header changes R1, R5 and AL; att = 2(15 - MAL) + (31 - AL) + 2(15 - LAL) = 2S + 1 - (AL & 1); VOL of the handbook.
#   A window anchors on its phase's last write (val= counts that record value; R1 is global): +2000..+100304 holds two whole cycles, +2000..+294912 five crossings at any phase (k = 4, d = 1024); P1 uses the tone_pan windows of its key-on.
#   P1 S = 0: per, lev 31 x 32768 = 1,015,808 (ASSUMED:LED-AUD-0009). P2 (P8-10: R1 $C8, AL $1D, R5 $F8): left S = 3 + 1 + 0 = 4, att 8: live, per (MAN), lev 31 x 8231 = 255,161; right S = 7 + 1 + 7 = 15: sil ASSUMED, disputed (mark=sum=15).
#   P3 R1 $C7: right S = 8 + 1 + 7 = 16; P4 R5 $00, P5 R1 $00: byte zero (sil MAN:P8-10). ao (MAN): left peaks fall for LAL F, E, D (P1, P6, P7: att 0, 2, 4), AL $1F, $1E (P1, P8), LMAL F, E (P1, P9); ae: P6 and P9, both att 2, equal (ASSUMED:LED-AUD-0009).
#   same_Y (MAN:P8-4): select 3 fully programmed with chON 0 (Y) against P1 with select 3 unwritten: the 256 samples from the first rising crossing of each window are equal. AF3 kills the one-sided silences.
scene	tone_atten	case=audio_tone_atten	role=literal
group	tone_atten	per_P1	form=ROWS	kind=period	class=MAN:P8-9+H8-23	kills=AF0,AF2,AF4,AF5,AF6
row	tone_atten	per_P1	anchor=ev:ch=2;reg=R4;val=$9F;nth=2;from=+51152;to=+295912;side=L	f=256;k=4;d=1024;r1=$FF;al=$1F;r5=$FF
row	tone_atten	per_P1	anchor=ev:ch=2;reg=R4;val=$9F;nth=2;from=+51152;to=+295912;side=R	f=256;k=4;d=1024;r1=$FF;al=$1F;r5=$FF
group	tone_atten	lev_P1	form=ROWS	kind=levels_exact	class=ASSUMED:LED-AUD-0009	kills=AF0,AF5,AF6
